  <p class="note rv">This project combined SEO and paid search under one owner, so every page change was judged by one question: does it help a driver find the right tyre and buy it online?</p>

  <section class="story rv">
    <h2><span class="mono">01</span>The challenge</h2>
    <div class="txt">
      <p>Tyres Online sells tyres online in a market full of marketplaces and big retail chains. “Tyres online” was the term that mattered most — high intent and high volume — and the site wasn’t close to winning it.</p>
      <p>Product discovery was weak too: shoppers search by size, brand and vehicle, and the category and product pages weren’t built to match those searches.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story rv">
    <h2><span class="mono">02</span>The approach</h2>
    <div class="txt">
      <p>Fix the foundation first, then make every product and category page earn its place in search.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="k">1</div><h3>Technical SEO</h3><p>Audited crawling, indexation and site structure, then resolved the issues holding back the key commercial pages.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="k">2</div><h3>Product-page improvements</h3><p>Rewrote titles, descriptions and on-page content around how people actually search for tyres.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="k">3</div><h3>Long-tail strategy</h3><p>Built keyword clusters for sizes, brands and use cases to improve product discovery and category visibility.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="k">4</div><h3>Shopping & Search</h3><p>Restructured Google Shopping and Search campaigns so paid and organic covered each other’s gaps.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story rv">
    <h2><span class="mono">03</span>The outcome</h2>
    <div class="txt">
      <p class="quote">#1 for the head term, 45% more organic traffic and 18% more online sales — in the first three months.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:20px">Paid search got more efficient at the same time: ROAS rose by 40% and cost per conversion dropped by 25%.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

